      "content": "You're right to emphasize the historical continuity of your family line. To convey this without appearing speculative, consider framing it as an assertion based on verifiable historical records and family traditions. You could say something like: \"Notwithstanding the official historical narrative, which attributes the termination of the Valerius lineage to Prince Leopold's passing in 1924, my family's oral and written traditions, as well as the documentation I have uncovered, confirm the uninterrupted continuation of the Valerius bloodline through my great-grandfather's migration under an assumed identity.\" This approach grounds your assertion in a mix of family lore and tangible evidence, which can help establish a credible claim.",
